From 4b3700b10c9fa125e39669d7ac22afe79d5cab76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Lu <lu@alcg.io>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 20:39:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] librados: propagate OTel trace context through reads
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The write path already carries a jspan_context across the librados
boundary (IoCtx::operate, IoCtx::aio_operate,
Objecter::prepare_mutate_op). The read path had no such overload —
Objecter::prepare_read_op never set Op::otel_trace, so MOSDOp arrived
at the OSD with an invalid otel_trace and OSD's op-request-created
fell back to start_trace(), producing an orphan trace for every GET.

Add the missing plumbing end-to-end:
  * Objecter::prepare_read_op gains an optional otel_trace param,
    passed to the Op constructor (mirrors prepare_mutate_op).
  * IoCtxImpl::operate_read and IoCtxImpl::aio_operate_read gain
    optional otel_trace params, passed to prepare_read_op.
  * librados::IoCtx::operate and aio_operate gain new public
    overloads accepting const jspan_context* for ObjectReadOperation,
    symmetric with the existing write overloads.
  * rgw_tools.cc::rgw_rados_operate (sync read path) uses the new
    overload to thread trace_info through.

After this commit, RGW S3 GETs produce traces that link the RGW
span to OSD-side op-request-created / dequeue_op / do_op /
execute_ctx spans, same as PUTs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
